        "is_set": true,
        "red": 1.0,
        "green": 0.0
      }
    },
    "kernel_output": {
      "type": "value",
      "data": {
        "is_set": true,
        "red": 1.0,
        "green": 0.0
      }
    },
    "comparison": {
      "equal": true,
      "differences": []
    },
    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantities on both sides. Bridge: isShapeColorSet true, and shapeColor's red within 1e-5 of 1.0 and green within 1e-5 of 0.0. The test asserts red and green and never blue or alpha, which is why the record holds two channels. Kernel: XCAFDoc_ColorTool IsSet true, and GetColor after SetColor(1, 0, 0, alpha 1) read back rgba (1, 0, 0, 1) exactly (printed %.17g); blue 0 and alpha 1 are not compared because the test does not assert them. Kernel values are from the supplementary probe, which runs the test's own scenario through the XCAFDoc_ColorTool / XCAFDoc_LayerTool calls the bridge makes.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-xcaf-xde-color-layer-parity/"
  },
